BIB                  6         26
REACTION   (96-CM-244(N,G)96-CM-245,,RYL,,MSC) EAR1 Sample A
           Capture yield for all the isotopes in the sample
            (Pu-240, Am-243, Cm-244, Cm-245, Cm-246).
SAMPLE     *Sample A
           This sample consists of two pellets and contains
            approximately 0.8 mg of Cm-244 and 0.4 mg of Pu-240.
           The absolute masses of the different isotopes are not
            precisely known; however, the isotopic mole fractions
            at the time of the measurement (summer 2017) were
            determined and are presented in the table below.
           These values were derived from the isotopic evolution,
            taking into account concentrations measured in 2010 by
            Kimura (2012) and radioactive decay.
           Isotopic abundances in percent during the Cm nTOF
            measurement campaign in August 2017:
           (94-PU-240,ENR=0.308) 30.8 +/- 0.6%
           (95-AM-243,ENR=0.006)  0.6 +/- 0.1%
           (96-CM-244,ENR=0.599) 59.9 +/- 1.1%
           (96-CM-245,ENR=0.024)  2.4 +/- 0.3%
           (96-CM-246,ENR=0.063)  6.3 +/- 0.3%
DETECTOR   (BAF2) TAC detector formed of 40 BaF2 crystals
           The same efficiency can be used for all the actinides
            in the sample.
METHOD     (TOF) Flight path length of 185.6+/-0.1 m.
ERR-ANALYS (ERR-S) Counting statistics
STATUS     (TABLE,,V.Alcayne+,J,ANE,227,111977,2026) Fig.A.11
